  "conventions": [
    "Procedural code (s. 531 BNSS): investigation_started_on, else fir_date, else arrest_date (flagged). Offence date decides only IPC/BNS for the punishment.",
    "Default bail: 90 days only for death, life or a minimum term of ten years or more (minimum-term reading of Rakesh Kumar Paul v. State of Assam, 2017); 60 days otherwise. BNSS cases with a maximum of ten years or more and no minimum carry a 'BNSS wording differs' note; the alert stays at day 60.",
    "Day counting: the first remand date is day 1 (arrest date if no remand date, flagged). Day N ends on remand + N - 1; the right accrues on remand + N if no chargesheet is filed by then.",
    "Chargesheet filed on or before day N: no default bail. Application made on or after the accrual date and before the chargesheet: availed. Chargesheet on or after the accrual date with no application before it: right lost.",
    "Special statutes: NDPS s. 36A(4) 180 days (extension up to 365), UAPA s. 43D(2) 90 days (extension up to 180). An extension is applied only when an order dated on or before the last day of the base period is entered.",
    "s. 479 BNSS for every undertrial: maximum x 365.25 x 1/3 (first-time offender) or 1/2, plus any delay caused by the accused; rounded up to whole days; counted from the arrest date (day 1) over all detention periods; the date given is the first day after the threshold is completed. Death or life: excluded. Other cases pending: excluded under s. 479(2).",
    "s. 436A CrPC (one-half; excludes only death) is shown as an alternative citation where the case began under the CrPC.",
    "Several sections: 90 days if any section qualifies; the s. 479 maximum is the highest maximum; any death or life section excludes s. 479."
  ],
